    {
      "id": "claim_26ef2e8928ec4ab1b495effddb7e1f42",
      "statement": "Route registration is handled by `build_routes` in `local_routes.py`, which converts resolved `paths` and `functions` into a list of `RouteInfo` objects sorted by specificity (`routes.sort(key=lambda r: r.is_greedy)`) so non-greedy exact routes and function URL routes (`/__fn/<name>`) are registered before greedy catch-all routes (`{path:path}`), preventing Starlette route shadowing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/critiques/local-lambda-execution-critique.md#L31-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba7dce0eccc07e2c8c15d2032cba7f8ccf207129dd005ce7f1bab6fb3f8b2760:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/specs/local-lambda-execution.md#L264-L275",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad5016f66cb46ee03faefdcb6cb7584b78ccad746574a94e6624541dcdb53881:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/easysam/local_routes.py#L5-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:268b8141dc8b10dc34d42dd8d30edec27795d8fdc52b3d366fef28deec1d2956:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c867e3a1908d4fdb98b1d6f5935162fc",
      "statement": "Greedy routes (where `greedy: true` or the path ends with `/`) are expanded into two `RouteInfo` entries: an exact route (trailing slash stripped) and a catch-all route (`{path:path}`), with the catch-all's `resource_path` set to `<api_path>/{proxy+}` so the event builder can map `{path:path}` to `pathParameters['proxy']` for AWS parity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/specs/local-lambda-execution.md#L57-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47f85499abbd2d939f858501692fcd1efda124025a4130dec852f27b622986eb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/easysam/local_routes.py#L28-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f901eaf43924e5f2a0e293665a85d0fc4bac37bdb8262231e5a974240ee052bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fdb61295ecfa4a7bb82dc40cd4e98243",
      "statement": "Per-request environment variable mutations are serialized via a module-level `asyncio.Lock()` (`_invocation_lock`) in `local_server.py`: the route handler reads the request body and builds the event *outside* the lock, then acquires the lock to set per-function envvars (saving originals), invoke the handler, and restore envvars in a `try...finally` block — guaranteeing envvar restoration and lock release even on unhandled exceptions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/codereviews/2026-08-04_local-mode_review.md#L27-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74a2af3a0f067d0806da033af84b284617e003e80f829c87bb52404a5596836a:"
        },
        {
